---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, apps, href } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Support" description="Get help or share an idea.">
  <section class="wrap section narrow">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="lead">Something not working, or an idea to make an app better? We read everything.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href={site.contactHref}>Email {site.contactEmail}</a></p>
    <p class="muted">Tell us which app, what device and browser you are using, and what you expected to happen. A screenshot helps.</p>

    <h2>Quick answers</h2>
    <h3>What is a PWA, and is it a real app?</h3>
    <p>A PWA (progressive web app) is a website that can be installed. Once you add it to your Home Screen or desktop it has its own icon, opens like any other app and works offline. The difference is that it comes from a link instead of an app store. <a href={href('install/')}>Read more</a>.</p>
    <h3>Why can't I find the app in the App Store or Google Play?</h3>
    <p>These apps are not in a store. You open the link and install them straight from your browser, which is why there is no download and why they update by themselves.</p>
    <h3>How do I put an app on my Home Screen?</h3>
    <p>See <a href={href('install/')}>How to install</a>.</p>
    <h3>Will it work without internet?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Once an app has opened once, it works offline, and it syncs when you are back online.</p>
    <h3>I cleared my browser and my information is gone.</h3>
    <p>Heirloom, Family Game Night and FishLog keep what you enter on your device, so clearing the browser's site data removes it. Installing the app to your Home Screen helps protect it. Simple Kennel and Coach Board, and FishLog if you signed in, save your information to your account, so sign back in and it syncs back down.</p>
    <h3>An app shows an old version.</h3>
    <p>Close it completely and open it again, and tap the "Update" prompt when it appears.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
